>In article <1993Jan11.202426.11531@cs.cornell.edu> bau@cs.cornell.edu (David Bau) writes:
>>creatures, including a tengu or two, and I got teleport control.  But I
>>couldn't use ^T to force myself to teleport - I had to wait until it happened
>>randomly.  But I kept on playing and eating more teleporting creatures,
>>and eventually, I found I was able to ^T, making the game much easier!
>>
>>I've never gotten the ability again.  How does it happen?  Do I have to
>>eat lots of n's and l's?  or t's?  Or do I have to wait for my experience
>>to go up?
>
>Teleport ability and teleport control are two different attributes (a nice
>touch from the design team).  You can get either through rings or through
>intrinsics gained from food.  Eating things that teleport may help, and
>a tango with tengus might settle that unsettled feeling...

Actually, they are three different abilities.  Teleport at random (the
normal teleport intrinsic, gotten by rings, corpses, ...), Teleport at
will (using ^T to teleport - you get it when you get to a certain level),
and teleport control.

You can teleport at will if your experience level is >= 12 (8 for wizards).
